1 NOTE In 1700 Frederick allied himself with Russia and Poland in the Great 
2 CONT Northern War against Sweden, but he was soon compelled by Charles XII, 
2 CONT king of Sweden, to withdraw from the conflict and to promise not to 
2 CONT reenter it. After the defeat of Charles at Poltava (now in Ukraine) in 
2 CONT 1709, however, Frederick again declared war on Sweden, subsequently taking 
2 CONT the German duchy of Schleswig and participating with the Poles in the 
2 CONT invasion of the Swedish portion of Pomerania. By treaty in 1720 Frederick 
2 CONT agreed to return to Sweden all conquests made in the war, except for 
2 CONT Schleswig. Among the accomplishments of his reign was the freeing of the 
2 CONT peasants from serfdom in 1702.
