2 CONT To America 1850.
2 CONT
2 CONT They came to the United States, landing in New York after a voyage of ten weeks and three days. They went direct to Dane County, Wisconsin, but a year later moved to LaSalle County, Illinois, and bought a house and lot, and also s
2 CONC ome cattle, which they cared for while the sons worked on farms by the month. They had a family of four children - Anna M., Helen, Canute and Peter. In August, 1861, the sons enlisted in Company F, Thirty-sixth Illinois Infantry, 
2 CONC and Peter died in the hospital at Murfreesboro in February, 1864.
