0 @N6000000002322291638@ NOTE He became the first king of Prussia, who freed his domains from imperial
1 CONT suzerainty, and continued the policy of territorial aggrandizement begun by
1 CONT his father, Frederick William, the Great Elector. Prussia's elevation to a
1 CONT monarchy gave greater cohesion to the diverse and dispersed Hollenzollern
1 CONT lands, which were then turned into provinces. Only his son, Frederick William
1 CONT II, and his grandson, Frederick II the Great, were able to exploit Prussia's
1 CONT enhanced position to the full and transorm the new kingdom into greatness.
